    "updated_at": "2025-01-03T00:25:40Z",
    "body": "Gecko now [uses color rather than opacity for placeholder](https://hg.mozilla.org/mozilla-central/rev/aae10b80691a).\r\n\r\n@fvsch I think that https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/2561#issuecomment-569920124:\r\n\r\n> If a web developer wants to use the same style in all browsers and to normalize on an existing browser's styles, they would need to use one of these three options:\r\n> \r\n> ```css\r\n> /* Gecko style */\r\n> ::placeholder {\r\n>   color: inherit;\r\n>   opacity: 0.54;\r\n> }\r\n> \r\n> /* WebKit style */\r\n> ::placeholder {\r\n>   color: #9a9a9a;\r\n>   opacity: 1;\r\n> }\r\n> \r\n> /* Blink style */\r\n> ::placeholder {\r\n>   color: #757575;\r\n>   opacity: 1;\r\n> }\r\n> ```\r\n\r\n…can be updated to:\r\n\r\n```css\r\n/* Gecko style */\r\n::placeholder {\r\n\tcolor: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 54%, transparent);\r\n}\r\n\r\n/* WebKit style */\r\n::placeholder {\r\n\tcolor: #a9a9a9;\r\n}\r\n\r\n/* Blink style */\r\n::placeholder {\r\n\tcolor: #757575;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n(I also updated Webkit's color from `#9a9a9a` to the current `#a9a9a9`).",
